window.REV_FLIP=window.REV_FLIP||{};window.REV_FLIP["python-automation"]=[{"id":"python-automation-f0001","card":"q-python-automation-001-1-course-scope-and-libraries","sec":"python-automation-s002","q":"What is the goal of the Python automation course, and which topics does it cover?","a":"<p>The goal is to automate tedious, repetitive tasks with Python. Topics: file manipulation, input validation, error handling, web scraping, browser interaction and API usage.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0002","card":"q-python-automation-001-1-course-scope-and-libraries","sec":"python-automation-s002","q":"What should you already know before starting the Python automation course?","a":"<p>Python syntax and logic, data types, functions, conditionals and loops, file and directory paths, and basic command-line use.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0003","card":"q-python-automation-001-1-course-scope-and-libraries","sec":"python-automation-s002","q":"In Python automation, which libraries handle the OS interface, file paths and running CLI commands?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><code>os</code> and <code>pathlib</code>: OS interface and file paths.</li>\n  <li><code>subprocess</code>: run CLI commands from Python.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0004","card":"q-python-automation-001-1-course-scope-and-libraries","sec":"python-automation-s002","q":"Which Python libraries parse CSV, JSON, XML and text patterns?","a":"<p><code>csv</code>, <code>json</code>, <code>xml.etree.ElementTree</code> and <code>re</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0005","card":"q-python-automation-001-1-course-scope-and-libraries","sec":"python-automation-s002","q":"Which libraries do Python automation scripts use for input validation, HTTP requests and HTML parsing?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><code>pyinputplus</code>: input validation.</li>\n  <li><code>requests</code>: HTTP requests.</li>\n  <li><code>BeautifulSoup</code>: HTML parsing.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0006","card":"q-python-automation-001-1-course-scope-and-libraries","sec":"python-automation-s002","q":"Which libraries do Python automation scripts use for browser automation and for loading secrets from <code>.env</code>?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><code>selenium</code> and <code>webdriver_manager</code>: browser automation.</li>\n  <li><code>python-dotenv</code>: load secrets from <code>.env</code>.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0007","card":"q-python-automation-002-2-reading-and-writing-files","sec":"python-automation-s003","q":"When you split a line like <code>name age P/F</code> in Python, which index holds which field?","a":"<p><code>.split()</code> splits on whitespace by default. Index 0 is the name, 1 the age, 2 the pass/fail flag.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0008","card":"q-python-automation-002-2-reading-and-writing-files","sec":"python-automation-s003","q":"How do you print only the passing lines of a drive test results file in Python?","a":"<p>Open the file in <code>\"r\"</code> mode, split each line, and print it when index 2 is <code>\"P\"</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>inputFile = open(&quot;inputFile.txt&quot;, &quot;r&quot;)\nfor line in inputFile:\n    line_split = line.split()\n    if line_split[2] == &quot;P&quot;:\n        print(line)\ninputFile.close()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0009","card":"q-python-automation-002-2-reading-and-writing-files","sec":"python-automation-s003","q":"How do you route each line of an input file into a pass file or a fail file in Python?","a":"<p>Open the input in <code>\"r\"</code> and both output files in <code>\"w\"</code>. Write each line to the pass file if index 2 is <code>\"P\"</code>, else to the fail file. Close all three files.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>for line in inputFile:\n    line_split = line.split()\n    if line_split[2] == &quot;P&quot;:\n        passFile.write(line)\n    else:\n        failFile.write(line)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0010","card":"q-python-automation-002-2-reading-and-writing-files","sec":"python-automation-s003","q":"What is the difference between file modes <code>\"r\"</code> and <code>\"w\"</code> in Python?","a":"<p><code>\"r\"</code> opens the file read-only. <code>\"w\"</code> creates the file, or overwrites it if it already exists.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0011","card":"q-python-automation-002-2-reading-and-writing-files","sec":"python-automation-s003","q":"Why should you call <code>.close()</code> on every file you open in Python, and what is the alternative?","a":"<p>Closing avoids unintended changes and leaks. A <code>with open(...) as f:</code> block closes the file for you.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0012","card":"q-python-automation-002-2-reading-and-writing-files","sec":"python-automation-s003","q":"Where should you save a Python script that reads files by relative path?","a":"<p>In the directory that holds the files, so the relative paths resolve.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0013","card":"q-python-automation-003-3-running-cli-commands-with-subprocess","sec":"python-automation-s004","q":"What does <code>subprocess</code> do in Python, and how is the command passed to <code>check_call()</code>?","a":"<p><code>subprocess</code> connects Python to the command line. <code>check_call()</code> runs an executable and waits for it to finish. The command is a list where each element is one terminal argument.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0014","card":"q-python-automation-003-3-running-cli-commands-with-subprocess","sec":"python-automation-s004","q":"How do you run <code>example.py</code> five times from another Python script?","a":"<p>Loop five times and call <code>subprocess.check_call</code> with the command as a list.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import subprocess\n\nfor i in range(5):\n    subprocess.check_call([&quot;python3&quot;, &quot;example.py&quot;])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0015","card":"q-python-automation-003-3-running-cli-commands-with-subprocess","sec":"python-automation-s004","q":"What happens when a command run by <code>subprocess.check_call</code> exits with a non-zero status?","a":"<p>It raises <code>CalledProcessError</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0016","card":"q-python-automation-003-3-running-cli-commands-with-subprocess","sec":"python-automation-s004","q":"How do you run the <code>practice.py</code> script that calls <code>subprocess.check_call</code>?","a":"<p>Run <code>python3 practice.py</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0017","card":"q-python-automation-004-4-organizing-files-by-type","sec":"python-automation-s005","q":"What does the Python file-organizer script do with the files in the current directory?","a":"<p>It sorts them into category folders by extension. Unknown types go to <code>MISC</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0018","card":"q-python-automation-004-4-organizing-files-by-type","sec":"python-automation-s005","q":"How does the file-organizer script map categories to file extensions?","a":"<p>With a dictionary named <code>SUBDIRECTORIES</code> whose keys are the category names and whose values are lists of extensions.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>SUBDIRECTORIES = {\n    &quot;DOCUMENTS&quot;: [&#x27;.pdf&#x27;, &#x27;.rtf&#x27;, &#x27;.txt&#x27;],\n    &quot;AUDIOS&quot;: [&#x27;.m4a&#x27;, &#x27;.m4b&#x27;, &#x27;.mp3&#x27;],\n    &quot;VIDEOS&quot;: [&#x27;.mov&#x27;, &#x27;.avi&#x27;, &#x27;.mp4&#x27;],\n    &quot;IMAGES&quot;: [&#x27;.jpg&#x27;, &#x27;.jpeg&#x27;, &#x27;.png&#x27;]\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0019","card":"q-python-automation-004-4-organizing-files-by-type","sec":"python-automation-s005","q":"How does <code>pickDirectory</code> choose the category for a file extension in the Python file organizer?","a":"<p>It loops over the dictionary and returns the category whose suffix list contains the value. If none matches, it returns <code>\"MISC\"</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def pickDirectory(value):\n    for category, suffixes in SUBDIRECTORIES.items():\n        if value in suffixes:\n            return category\n    return &quot;MISC&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0020","card":"q-python-automation-004-4-organizing-files-by-type","sec":"python-automation-s005","q":"What are the steps of <code>organizeDirectory</code> in the Python file organizer?","a":"<ol>\n  <li>Iterate the current directory with <code>os.scandir()</code> and skip directories.</li>\n  <li>Get the lower-case extension with <code>Path(item).suffix</code>.</li>\n  <li>Pick the category with <code>pickDirectory</code>.</li>\n  <li>Create the folder with <code>.mkdir()</code> if it is missing.</li>\n  <li>Move the file with <code>.rename()</code>.</li>\n</ol>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0021","card":"q-python-automation-004-4-organizing-files-by-type","sec":"python-automation-s005","q":"What do <code>os.scandir()</code>, <code>Path(item).suffix</code>, <code>.mkdir()</code> and <code>.rename()</code> do in the file organizer?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><code>os.scandir()</code>: iterates the current directory.</li>\n  <li><code>Path(item).suffix</code>: gives the extension.</li>\n  <li><code>.mkdir()</code>: creates a folder.</li>\n  <li><code>.rename()</code>: moves the file.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0022","card":"q-python-automation-004-4-organizing-files-by-type","sec":"python-automation-s005","q":"Why does the file organizer call <code>.lower()</code> on the suffix?","a":"<p>It makes extension matching case-insensitive.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0023","card":"q-python-automation-004-4-organizing-files-by-type","sec":"python-automation-s005","q":"How do you test the file organizer's lookup before moving any files, and how do you check the result?","a":"<p>Call <code>pickDirectory(\".pdf\")</code>, which gives <code>DOCUMENTS</code>, before running <code>organizeDirectory()</code>. Check the result with <code>ls</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>print(pickDirectory(&quot;.pdf&quot;))  # DOCUMENTS (test the function before running everything)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0024","card":"q-python-automation-005-5-parsing-data-files-txt-csv-json-xml","sec":"python-automation-s006","q":"What pattern do all four file parsers (txt, CSV, JSON, XML) share in Python?","a":"<p>Open the file, read it, and convert it into Python structures.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0025","card":"q-python-automation-005-5-parsing-data-files-txt-csv-json-xml","sec":"python-automation-s006","q":"How do you parse a plain text file of comma-separated values in Python?","a":"<p>Read the whole file in a <code>with</code> block and split it on <code>\", \"</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>with open(file_path, &quot;r&quot;) as file:\n    data = file.read()\n\nparsed_data = data.split(&quot;, &quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0026","card":"q-python-automation-005-5-parsing-data-files-txt-csv-json-xml","sec":"python-automation-s006","q":"How do you read a CSV file in Python, skip the header row and convert a numeric column to <code>int</code>?","a":"<p>Use <code>csv.reader</code>, call <code>next()</code> once to consume the headers, then cast the column in each row.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>csv_reader = csv.reader(file)\nheaders = next(csv_reader)\nfor row in csv_reader:\n    row[1] = int(row[1])\n    print(row)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0027","card":"q-python-automation-005-5-parsing-data-files-txt-csv-json-xml","sec":"python-automation-s006","q":"Why do you cast numeric values after reading a CSV file in Python?","a":"<p>CSV values are strings. <code>next(csv_reader)</code> consumes the header row, and numbers must be cast.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0028","card":"q-python-automation-005-5-parsing-data-files-txt-csv-json-xml","sec":"python-automation-s006","q":"How do you parse a JSON file into a Python dict?","a":"<p>Read the file as a string and pass it to <code>json.loads</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>parsed_data = json.loads(data)\nprint(&quot;apples quantity:&quot;, parsed_data[&quot;apples&quot;])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0029","card":"q-python-automation-005-5-parsing-data-files-txt-csv-json-xml","sec":"python-automation-s006","q":"What is the difference between <code>json.loads</code> and <code>json.load</code>?","a":"<p><code>json.loads</code> takes a string. <code>json.load</code> takes a file object.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0030","card":"q-python-automation-005-5-parsing-data-files-txt-csv-json-xml","sec":"python-automation-s006","q":"How do you parse an XML file with <code>ElementTree</code> and find the items priced higher than 6.00?","a":"<p>Parse the file, get the root, loop over <code>findall</code>, read <code>.text</code> of the children and cast the price to <code>float</code> before comparing.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>tree = ET.parse(&quot;groceries.xml&quot;)\nroot = tree.getroot()\nfor item in root.findall(&quot;grocery_item&quot;):\n    name = item.find(&quot;name&quot;).text\n    price = item.find(&quot;price&quot;).text\n    if float(price) &gt; 6.00:\n        items_over_six.append(name)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0031","card":"q-python-automation-005-5-parsing-data-files-txt-csv-json-xml","sec":"python-automation-s006","q":"Why must you cast XML values before comparing them in Python?","a":"<p>Values from <code>.text</code> are strings, so cast them (for example <code>float(price)</code>) before comparing.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0032","card":"q-python-automation-006-6-regular-expressions","sec":"python-automation-s007","q":"What are regular expressions used for in Python automation?","a":"<p>To extract structured data, such as phone numbers and emails, from text.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0033","card":"q-python-automation-006-6-regular-expressions","sec":"python-automation-s007","q":"How do you build a regex that matches a phone number like <code>XXX-XXX-XXXX</code> in Python?","a":"<p>Use <code>re.compile()</code> with <code>\\d</code> for each digit.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>phoneNumRegex = re.compile(r&quot;\\d\\d\\d-\\d\\d\\d-\\d\\d\\d\\d&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0034","card":"q-python-automation-006-6-regular-expressions","sec":"python-automation-s007","q":"What does <code>\\d</code> match in a Python regular expression?","a":"<p>One digit.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0035","card":"q-python-automation-006-6-regular-expressions","sec":"python-automation-s007","q":"What does <code>.search()</code> return in Python's <code>re</code> module, and what must you do before calling <code>.group()</code>?","a":"<p>It returns the first match or <code>None</code>. Test the result first. <code>.group()</code> returns the matched text.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>result = phoneNumRegex.search(example)\nif result:\n    print(&quot;Phone number found:&quot;, result.group())\n    print(&quot;Area code:&quot;, result.group()[0:3])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0036","card":"q-python-automation-007-7-input-validation-with-pyinputplus","sec":"python-automation-s008","q":"Why validate input in a Python automation script?","a":"<p>It prevents bad data (financial loss from wrong amounts, exposure of sensitive data), protects data integrity, and gives users immediate feedback.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0037","card":"q-python-automation-007-7-input-validation-with-pyinputplus","sec":"python-automation-s008","q":"How does PyInputPlus handle invalid input?","a":"<p>It re-prompts until the input is valid.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0038","card":"q-python-automation-007-7-input-validation-with-pyinputplus","sec":"python-automation-s008","q":"How do you ask for an integer that must be at least 0 with PyInputPlus?","a":"<p>Use <code>pyip.inputInt</code> with the <code>min</code> option.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>result = pyip.inputInt(&quot;Enter the number of shopping bags you will need for your items:&quot;, min=0)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0039","card":"q-python-automation-007-7-input-validation-with-pyinputplus","sec":"python-automation-s008","q":"How do you show a lettered menu of choices with PyInputPlus?","a":"<p>Use <code>inputMenu</code> with <code>lettered=True</code> and <code>numbered=False</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>result = pyip.inputMenu([&quot;red&quot;, &quot;blue&quot;, &quot;green&quot;], lettered=True, numbered=False)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0040","card":"q-python-automation-007-7-input-validation-with-pyinputplus","sec":"python-automation-s008","q":"How do you check an email address with PyInputPlus?","a":"<p>Use <code>inputEmail</code> with a prompt string.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>result = pyip.inputEmail(&quot;Enter your email address:&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0041","card":"q-python-automation-007-7-input-validation-with-pyinputplus","sec":"python-automation-s008","q":"What do <code>inputInt()</code>, <code>inputMenu()</code> and <code>inputEmail()</code> do, and which options do they take?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Function</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Options</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>inputInt()</code></td><td>Integer input</td><td><code>min</code>, <code>max</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>inputMenu()</code></td><td>Pick from a list</td><td><code>lettered</code>, <code>numbered</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>inputEmail()</code></td><td>Email format check</td><td>prompt string</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0042","card":"q-python-automation-008-8-error-handling-and-assertions","sec":"python-automation-s009","q":"What are the benefits of error handling in Python?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Robustness: unexpected situations are handled gracefully.</li>\n  <li>User experience: informative messages instead of cryptic tracebacks.</li>\n  <li>Debugging efficiency: detailed error information.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0043","card":"q-python-automation-009-error-categories","sec":"python-automation-s010","q":"What are the three categories of errors in Python?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Description</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Syntax error</td><td>Code breaks language rules; program will not run</td><td>missing colon after <code>if x &gt; 5</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Runtime error (exception)</td><td>Raised while running</td><td><code>NameError</code>, <code>TypeError</code> and others</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Logical error</td><td>Runs but gives wrong results</td><td><code>range(5)</code> where <code>range(10)</code> was intended</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0044","card":"q-python-automation-009-error-categories","sec":"python-automation-s010","q":"What causes a <code>NameError</code> in Python, and what is an example?","a":"<p>A variable is used before it is defined, for example <code>print(x)</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0045","card":"q-python-automation-009-error-categories","sec":"python-automation-s010","q":"What causes a <code>TypeError</code> in Python, and what is an example?","a":"<p>The wrong type for the operation, for example <code>\"5\" + 5</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0046","card":"q-python-automation-009-error-categories","sec":"python-automation-s010","q":"What causes an <code>IndexError</code> in Python, and what is an example?","a":"<p>An index is out of range, for example <code>list[10]</code> on 5 items.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0047","card":"q-python-automation-009-error-categories","sec":"python-automation-s010","q":"What causes an <code>AttributeError</code> in Python, and what is an example?","a":"<p>The attribute or method does not exist, for example <code>string.append()</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0048","card":"q-python-automation-009-error-categories","sec":"python-automation-s010","q":"What causes a <code>ValueError</code> in Python, and what is an example?","a":"<p>The type is right but the value is wrong, for example <code>int(\"abc\")</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0049","card":"q-python-automation-009-error-categories","sec":"python-automation-s010","q":"What causes a <code>ZeroDivisionError</code> in Python, and what is an example?","a":"<p>Division by zero, for example <code>10 / 0</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0050","card":"q-python-automation-010-try-except","sec":"python-automation-s011","q":"How do you catch a non-integer input and a division by zero separately in Python?","a":"<p>Put the code in <code>try</code> and add one <code>except</code> per exception type.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>try:\n    number = int(input(&quot;Enter a number: &quot;))\n    result = 10 / number\n    print(&quot;The result is:&quot;, result)\nexcept ValueError:\n    print(&quot;You must enter a valid integer.&quot;)\nexcept ZeroDivisionError:\n    print(&quot;You cannot divide by zero.&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0051","card":"q-python-automation-010-try-except","sec":"python-automation-s011","q":"A Python script reads <code>int(input(\"Enter a number: \"))</code>, prints <code>10 / number</code>, and has <code>except ValueError</code> and <code>except ZeroDivisionError</code> branches. What happens for the inputs <code>5</code>, <code>0</code> and <code>abc</code>?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><code>5</code> prints <code>The result is: 2.0</code>.</li>\n  <li><code>0</code> hits the <code>ZeroDivisionError</code> branch.</li>\n  <li><code>abc</code> hits the <code>ValueError</code> branch.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0052","card":"q-python-automation-010-try-except","sec":"python-automation-s011","q":"What happens to execution when an exception occurs inside a Python <code>try</code> block?","a":"<p>Execution jumps to the matching <code>except</code>. If no exception occurs, the <code>except</code> blocks are skipped.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0053","card":"q-python-automation-010-try-except","sec":"python-automation-s011","q":"Should you catch bare <code>Exception</code> in Python error handling?","a":"<p>No. Catch specific exception types.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0054","card":"q-python-automation-011-assert-catches-logical-errors","sec":"python-automation-s012","q":"What does <code>assert condition, \"message\"</code> do in Python?","a":"<p>It raises <code>AssertionError</code> with the message when the condition is False.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0055","card":"q-python-automation-011-assert-catches-logical-errors","sec":"python-automation-s012","q":"How can <code>assert</code> catch the bug in a script that uses <code>years.reverse()</code> to sort a list?","a":"<p><code>reverse()</code> only reverses the order, it does not sort. An assertion on the first and last elements fails with <code>AssertionError: First element is greater than last element.</code></p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>years.reverse()   # wrong: reverses order, does not sort\nassert years[0] &lt;= years[-1], &quot;First element is greater than last element.&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0056","card":"q-python-automation-011-assert-catches-logical-errors","sec":"python-automation-s012","q":"A Python script sorts a list of years with <code>years.reverse()</code> and then asserts <code>years[0] &lt;= years[-1]</code>, which fails. How do you fix it?","a":"<p>Use <code>years.sort()</code>. The list becomes <code>[1912, 1920, ..., 1996]</code> and the assertion passes.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0057","card":"q-python-automation-011-assert-catches-logical-errors","sec":"python-automation-s012","q":"Is <code>assert</code> a replacement for input validation in Python?","a":"<p>No. It is a debugging tool for checking assumptions.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0058","card":"q-python-automation-011-assert-catches-logical-errors","sec":"python-automation-s012","q":"When do you use <code>try/except</code> and when <code>assert</code> in Python?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Technique</th><th>Use for</th><th>Syntax</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>try/except</td><td>Runtime exceptions</td><td><code>try: ... except ErrorType: ...</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>assert</td><td>Logic and assumptions</td><td><code>assert condition, \"message\"</code></td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0059","card":"q-python-automation-012-9-web-scraping-with-requests-and-beautif","sec":"python-automation-s013","q":"What is web scraping, and why use it?","a":"<p>It extracts large volumes of data from websites quickly, a job that is impractical to do manually.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0060","card":"q-python-automation-012-9-web-scraping-with-requests-and-beautif","sec":"python-automation-s013","q":"What is BeautifulSoup?","a":"<p>The Python library for pulling data out of HTML and XML.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0061","card":"q-python-automation-012-9-web-scraping-with-requests-and-beautif","sec":"python-automation-s013","q":"What are the use cases for web scraping?","a":"<p>Data extraction (prices, product details, headlines), parsing complex page structures, automated testing (element existence, layout), price monitoring, market and academic research, and collecting machine learning training data.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0062","card":"q-python-automation-013-html-basics","sec":"python-automation-s014","q":"What is the basic structure of an HTML page?","a":"<p><code>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;</code> declares the document type. <code>&lt;html&gt;</code> is the root. <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> holds metadata and <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> holds visible content.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">HTML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0063","card":"q-python-automation-013-html-basics","sec":"python-automation-s014","q":"What goes in the <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> of an HTML page, and is it displayed?","a":"<p>Metadata such as the title, CSS links, author and keywords. It is not displayed.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0064","card":"q-python-automation-013-html-basics","sec":"python-automation-s014","q":"What do <code>&lt;h1&gt;</code> to <code>&lt;h6&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;p&gt;</code> mean in HTML?","a":"<p><code>&lt;h1&gt;</code> to <code>&lt;h6&gt;</code> are headings, from largest to smallest. <code>&lt;p&gt;</code> is a paragraph.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0065","card":"q-python-automation-013-html-basics","sec":"python-automation-s014","q":"Why learn HTML basics for Python automation?","a":"<p>HTML knowledge is the base for scraping, Selenium and testing.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0066","card":"q-python-automation-014-inspecting-the-page","sec":"python-automation-s015","q":"How do you find which tag and class to scrape on a web page?","a":"<p>Right-click the page and choose Inspect, hover over elements to highlight them, and note the tag and class name. Check several items to confirm the pattern is consistent.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0067","card":"q-python-automation-014-inspecting-the-page","sec":"python-automation-s015","q":"In the feedbooks catalog example, which classes mark the cover, title, author and price?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Cover image: <code>b-item-cover</code></li>\n  <li>Title: <code>block__item-title</code></li>\n  <li>Author: <code>block__item-author</code></li>\n  <li>Price: <code>block__item-price</code></li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0068","card":"q-python-automation-015-request-parse-extract","sec":"python-automation-s016","q":"How do you request a page and parse its HTML with <code>requests</code> and BeautifulSoup?","a":"<p>Call <code>requests.get</code> with an <code>Accept</code> header for HTML, then pass <code>response.text</code> to <code>BeautifulSoup</code> with <code>\"html.parser\"</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>response = requests.get(url, headers={&quot;Accept&quot;: &quot;text/html&quot;})\nparsed_response = BeautifulSoup(response.text, &quot;html.parser&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0069","card":"q-python-automation-015-request-parse-extract","sec":"python-automation-s016","q":"What does the <code>Accept: text/html</code> header do in a scraping request?","a":"<p>It asks for an HTML-only response.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0070","card":"q-python-automation-015-request-parse-extract","sec":"python-automation-s016","q":"What are <code>response.text</code> and <code>\"html.parser\"</code> in BeautifulSoup scraping?","a":"<p><code>response.text</code> is the raw HTML. <code>\"html.parser\"</code> is Python's built-in parser.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0071","card":"q-python-automation-015-request-parse-extract","sec":"python-automation-s016","q":"How do you print the title text of every book on a catalog page with BeautifulSoup?","a":"<p>Use <code>find_all</code> with the tag and class, then print each element's <code>.text</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>titles = parsed_response.find_all(&quot;a&quot;, class_=&quot;block__item-title&quot;)\nfor title in titles:\n    print(title.text)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0072","card":"q-python-automation-015-request-parse-extract","sec":"python-automation-s016","q":"What do <code>.find()</code>, <code>.find_all()</code>, <code>.text</code> and <code>.prettify()</code> do in BeautifulSoup?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>.find(tag, class_=...)</code></td><td>First matching element</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>.find_all(tag, class_=...)</code></td><td>All matching elements. Note the underscore in <code>class_</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>.text</code></td><td>Text content of an element</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>.prettify()</code></td><td>Indented HTML for readability</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0073","card":"q-python-automation-015-request-parse-extract","sec":"python-automation-s016","q":"Why is the class argument written <code>class_</code> in BeautifulSoup?","a":"<p>The method name uses an underscore: <code>class_</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0074","card":"q-python-automation-016-scraping-multiple-pages","sec":"python-automation-s017","q":"How do you scrape several pages whose URL differs only by a page number?","a":"<p>Loop over the numbers, build the URL for each, request it, and pause between requests.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>for page_number in range(1, 4):   # pages 1, 2, 3 (end is excluded)\n    url = &quot;https://www.feedbooks.com/publicdomain/browse/top?lang=en&amp;page=&quot; + str(page_number)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0075","card":"q-python-automation-016-scraping-multiple-pages","sec":"python-automation-s017","q":"Why call <code>sleep(1)</code> between requests in a scraping loop?","a":"<p>So you do not overwhelm the server.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>sleep(1)   # do not overwhelm the server</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0076","card":"q-python-automation-016-scraping-multiple-pages","sec":"python-automation-s017","q":"How do you collect cleaned title text from a list of elements in a scraping loop?","a":"<p>Map over the elements with a lambda that strips the text.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>print(&quot;\\nBook Titles:&quot;, list(map(lambda x: x.text.strip(), title_elements)))</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0077","card":"q-python-automation-016-scraping-multiple-pages","sec":"python-automation-s017","q":"What are the shorter equivalents of string concatenation with <code>str()</code> and of <code>map</code>/<code>lambda</code> when scraping pages?","a":"<p>An f-string for the URL and a list comprehension for the text.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>url = f&quot;https://example.com/page={page_number}&quot;               # f-string instead of str() concatenation\n[element.text.strip() for element in elements]                 # list comprehension instead of map/lambda</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0078","card":"q-python-automation-017-error-handling-and-troubleshooting","sec":"python-automation-s018","q":"How do you make a scraping request fail loudly on HTTP errors and catch the error?","a":"<p>Call <code>response.raise_for_status()</code>, which raises on 4xx/5xx, inside a <code>try</code> that catches <code>requests.exceptions.RequestException</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>try:\n    response = requests.get(url, headers={&quot;Accept&quot;: &quot;text/html&quot;})\n    response.raise_for_status()   # raises on 4xx/5xx status\n    soup = BeautifulSoup(response.text, &quot;html.parser&quot;)\nexcept requests.exceptions.RequestException as e:\n    print(f&quot;Error: {e}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0079","card":"q-python-automation-017-error-handling-and-troubleshooting","sec":"python-automation-s018","q":"What are the causes and fixes when a BeautifulSoup scrape returns empty results or misses data?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Issue</th><th>Cause</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Empty results</td><td>Wrong tag or class name</td><td>Re-inspect the HTML</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Missing data</td><td>Content loaded by JavaScript</td><td><code>requests</code> only gets static HTML; use Selenium</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0080","card":"q-python-automation-017-error-handling-and-troubleshooting","sec":"python-automation-s018","q":"What are the causes and fixes for connection errors and rate limiting when scraping?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Issue</th><th>Cause</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Connection errors</td><td>Server unavailable</td><td>Add error handling</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Rate limiting</td><td>Too many requests</td><td>Increase <code>sleep</code></td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0081","card":"q-python-automation-017-error-handling-and-troubleshooting","sec":"python-automation-s018","q":"What does being a good citizen mean when scraping a website?","a":"<p>Check <code>robots.txt</code> and the site's terms of service, add delays, and expect pages to change structure.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0082","card":"q-python-automation-018-10-selenium-browser-automation","sec":"python-automation-s019","q":"What is Selenium, and what is it used for?","a":"<p>An open-source framework that controls browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Safari) from Python through WebDriver. It simulates user actions (click, type, navigate) and scales from one task to full test suites. Use it for testing, scraping JavaScript-rendered content, filling forms, and QA.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0083","card":"q-python-automation-018-10-selenium-browser-automation","sec":"python-automation-s019","q":"Which imports does Selenium need for Chrome, Firefox and Safari?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Chrome: <code>ChromeService</code> and <code>ChromeDriverManager</code>.</li>\n  <li>Firefox: <code>FirefoxService</code> and <code>GeckoDriverManager</code>.</li>\n  <li>Safari: a built-in driver.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0084","card":"q-python-automation-018-10-selenium-browser-automation","sec":"python-automation-s019","q":"What does <code>webdriver_manager</code> do in Selenium?","a":"<p>It downloads the matching driver automatically, which avoids \"driver not found\" errors.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0085","card":"q-python-automation-019-filling-a-form","sec":"python-automation-s020","q":"How do you get the XPath of an element for Selenium?","a":"<p>Right-click the element in Inspect, then Copy, then Copy XPath.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0086","card":"q-python-automation-019-filling-a-form","sec":"python-automation-s020","q":"How do you start a Chrome browser with Selenium and open a page?","a":"<p>Create the driver with <code>ChromeService(ChromeDriverManager().install())</code>, maximize the window and call <code>get</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>driver = webdriver.Chrome(service=ChromeService(ChromeDriverManager().install()))\ndriver.maximize_window()\ndriver.get(url)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0087","card":"q-python-automation-019-filling-a-form","sec":"python-automation-s020","q":"How do you type into a text field with Selenium?","a":"<p>Find the element by XPath and call <code>send_keys</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>first_name = driver.find_element(By.XPATH, &#x27;//*[@id=&quot;input-firstname&quot;]&#x27;)\nfirst_name.send_keys(&quot;John&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0088","card":"q-python-automation-019-filling-a-form","sec":"python-automation-s020","q":"How do you select a radio button, tick a checkbox and submit a form with Selenium?","a":"<p>Find each element and call <code>click()</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>driver.find_element(By.XPATH, &#x27;//*[@id=&quot;newsletter-no&quot;]&#x27;).click()\ndriver.find_element(By.XPATH, &#x27;//*[@id=&quot;agree&quot;]&#x27;).click()\ndriver.find_element(By.XPATH, &#x27;//*[@id=&quot;submit&quot;]&#x27;).click()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0089","card":"q-python-automation-019-filling-a-form","sec":"python-automation-s020","q":"How do you scroll the page down 200 px with Selenium?","a":"<p>Run JavaScript with <code>execute_script</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>driver.execute_script(&quot;window.scrollTo(0, window.scrollY + 200)&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0090","card":"q-python-automation-019-filling-a-form","sec":"python-automation-s020","q":"Why call <code>driver.quit()</code> at the end of a Selenium script?","a":"<p>To close the browser and free resources.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>sleep(5)        # pause to view the result\ndriver.quit()   # always close the browser to free resources</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0091","card":"q-python-automation-020-drag-and-drop","sec":"python-automation-s021","q":"How do you drag one element onto another with Selenium?","a":"<p>Find the source and destination, then use <code>ActionChains</code> with <code>drag_and_drop</code> and <code>.perform()</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ActionChains(driver).drag_and_drop(source, destination).perform()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0092","card":"q-python-automation-020-drag-and-drop","sec":"python-automation-s021","q":"What does <code>ActionChains</code> do in Selenium?","a":"<p>It queues complex user interactions, and <code>.perform()</code> executes them.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0093","card":"q-python-automation-021-reference","sec":"python-automation-s022","q":"What do the main Selenium driver and element methods do?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>driver.get(url)</code></td><td>Load a page</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>driver.maximize_window()</code></td><td>Maximize the browser so elements are visible</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>driver.execute_script(js)</code></td><td>Run JavaScript (scrolling)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>driver.quit()</code></td><td>Close the browser</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>find_element(By.X, value)</code></td><td>Find one element</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>element.send_keys(\"text\")</code></td><td>Type into a field</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>element.click()</code></td><td>Click</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0094","card":"q-python-automation-021-reference","sec":"python-automation-s022","q":"Which locator strategies does Selenium offer, and which is preferred?","a":"<p><code>By.XPATH</code>, <code>By.ID</code>, <code>By.CLASS_NAME</code> and <code>By.CSS_SELECTOR</code>. XPath copied from the browser breaks when the page changes, so prefer IDs when available.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0095","card":"q-python-automation-021-reference","sec":"python-automation-s022","q":"What are the causes and fixes for common Selenium problems such as element not found, not clickable, stale element and driver not found?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Issue</th><th>Cause</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Element not found</td><td>Wrong XPath</td><td>Re-inspect and copy again</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Element not clickable</td><td>Not loaded yet</td><td>Use an explicit wait</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Stale element</td><td>Page refreshed</td><td>Find the element again</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Driver not found</td><td>Missing driver</td><td>Use <code>webdriver_manager</code></td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0096","card":"q-python-automation-022-11-selenium-waiting-strategies","sec":"python-automation-s023","q":"Why does Selenium need waiting strategies?","a":"<p>Modern sites load content asynchronously (Ajax). WebDriver may look for an element before it exists, which causes exceptions such as <code>ElementNotVisibleException</code> and failed runs. Waiting strategies pause until the element is ready.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0097","card":"q-python-automation-022-11-selenium-waiting-strategies","sec":"python-automation-s023","q":"What are the three Selenium waiting types and how do they differ?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Behavior</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Explicit wait</td><td>Waits until a specific condition is met, up to a timeout</td><td>Precise, recommended for dynamic content</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Implicit wait</td><td>Global wait for elements to be available</td><td>Simpler, less precise</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>sleep()</code></td><td>Always waits the full duration</td><td>Wasteful; fine only for viewing results while testing</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0098","card":"q-python-automation-022-11-selenium-waiting-strategies","sec":"python-automation-s023","q":"How do you set an implicit wait in Selenium?","a":"<p>Call <code>driver.implicitly_wait</code> with the seconds. It applies to every <code>find_element</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>driver.implicitly_wait(10)   # implicit: applies to every find_element, up to 10 s</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0099","card":"q-python-automation-023-explicit-wait","sec":"python-automation-s024","q":"How do you create an explicit wait in Selenium?","a":"<p>Create a <code>WebDriverWait</code> with the driver and the maximum seconds.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>wait = WebDriverWait(driver, 10)   # maximum 10 seconds</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0100","card":"q-python-automation-023-explicit-wait","sec":"python-automation-s024","q":"How do you click a button that appears only after a loading state in Selenium?","a":"<p>Use <code>wait.until</code> with <code>EC.element_to_be_clickable</code>, then click. A static element needs no wait.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>disable_button = wait.until(EC.element_to_be_clickable((By.XPATH, &#x27;//*[@id=&quot;btn-disable&quot;]&#x27;)))\ndisable_button.click()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0101","card":"q-python-automation-023-explicit-wait","sec":"python-automation-s024","q":"Why is <code>wait.until(...)</code> better than <code>sleep(10)</code> in Selenium?","a":"<p><code>wait.until(...)</code> proceeds as soon as the condition is true, so it can finish well before the timeout. <code>sleep(10)</code> always costs 10 seconds.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0102","card":"q-python-automation-023-explicit-wait","sec":"python-automation-s024","q":"What is the syntax of <code>wait.until</code> and what type is the locator?","a":"<p><code>wait.until(condition((locator_strategy, 'locator_value')))</code>. The locator is a tuple.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0103","card":"q-python-automation-024-expected-conditions","sec":"python-automation-s025","q":"What do the Selenium expected conditions <code>element_to_be_clickable</code> and <code>presence_of_element_located</code> mean?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><code>element_to_be_clickable</code>: visible and enabled (most common).</li>\n  <li><code>presence_of_element_located</code>: exists in the DOM (may be hidden).</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0104","card":"q-python-automation-024-expected-conditions","sec":"python-automation-s025","q":"What do the Selenium expected conditions <code>visibility_of_element_located</code>, <code>invisibility_of_element_located</code> and <code>text_to_be_present_in_element</code> mean?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><code>visibility_of_element_located</code>: visible.</li>\n  <li><code>invisibility_of_element_located</code>: not visible (for example a loader gone).</li>\n  <li><code>text_to_be_present_in_element</code>: given text appears.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0105","card":"q-python-automation-024-expected-conditions","sec":"python-automation-s025","q":"How do you wait for the text <code>Success</code> in an element with ID <code>message</code>, or for an element with class <code>success</code> to be visible?","a":"<p>Use <code>wait.until</code> with the matching condition.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>wait.until(EC.text_to_be_present_in_element((By.ID, &#x27;message&#x27;), &#x27;Success&#x27;))\nmessage = wait.until(EC.visibility_of_element_located((By.CLASS_NAME, &#x27;success&#x27;)))</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0106","card":"q-python-automation-024-expected-conditions","sec":"python-automation-s025","q":"When should you use explicit waits in Selenium?","a":"<p>For loading indicators, Ajax content, state changes (disabled to enabled), animations, and validation messages.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0107","card":"q-python-automation-025-timeouts-and-multiple-conditions","sec":"python-automation-s026","q":"How do you handle a Selenium wait that times out?","a":"<p>Catch <code>TimeoutException</code> around the <code>wait.until</code> call.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>except TimeoutException:\n    print(&quot;Element did not become clickable within timeout period&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0108","card":"q-python-automation-025-timeouts-and-multiple-conditions","sec":"python-automation-s026","q":"How do you proceed when either of two Selenium conditions is met?","a":"<p>Wrap them in <code>EC.any_of</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>element = wait.until(\n    EC.any_of(\n        EC.element_to_be_clickable((By.ID, &#x27;btn1&#x27;)),\n        EC.element_to_be_clickable((By.ID, &#x27;btn2&#x27;))\n    )\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0109","card":"q-python-automation-025-timeouts-and-multiple-conditions","sec":"python-automation-s026","q":"What are the causes and fixes for <code>TimeoutException</code>, a non-clickable element and a wrong condition in Selenium waits?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Issue</th><th>Cause</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>TimeoutException</code></td><td>Element never appears</td><td>Raise the timeout or check the locator</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Not clickable</td><td>Covered by an overlay</td><td>Wait for the overlay to disappear</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Wrong condition</td><td>Condition does not match the state</td><td>Pick the right <code>EC</code> method</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0110","card":"q-python-automation-026-12-working-with-apis","sec":"python-automation-s027","q":"What is an API and why use one in automation?","a":"<p>An API (Application Programming Interface) is a bridge between applications. It gives access to external data and services without reinventing them, supports real-time data (weather, stock prices), reuse, and integration between services.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0111","card":"q-python-automation-026-12-working-with-apis","sec":"python-automation-s027","q":"What are typical uses of APIs?","a":"<p>Weather, e-commerce product data, finance, social media and maps.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0112","card":"q-python-automation-027-get-with-parameters","sec":"python-automation-s028","q":"How do you send query parameters with <code>requests.get</code>?","a":"<p>Put them in a dict and pass it as <code>params</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>parameters = {&quot;upc&quot;: &quot;025000044908&quot;}   # query parameters as a dict\nresponse = requests.get(base_url, params=parameters)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0113","card":"q-python-automation-027-get-with-parameters","sec":"python-automation-s028","q":"How can you see the final URL and the raw body of a <code>requests</code> response?","a":"<p><code>response.url</code> holds the URL with the parameters. <code>response.text</code> holds the raw body.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>print(response.url)    # https://api.upcitemdb.com/prod/trial/lookup?upc=025000044908\nprint(response.text)   # raw response body</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0114","card":"q-python-automation-027-get-with-parameters","sec":"python-automation-s028","q":"Where do the base URL and parameter names of an API come from?","a":"<p>From the API documentation. Read the docs first.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0115","card":"q-python-automation-028-parsing-a-json-response","sec":"python-automation-s029","q":"How do you read the title and brand of the first item in a JSON API response?","a":"<p>Convert the text with <code>json.loads</code>, then navigate the nested keys and the list index.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>info = json.loads(response.text)   # JSON string to Python dict\nitem = info[&quot;items&quot;][0]            # navigate nested keys and list index\ntitle = item[&quot;title&quot;]\nbrand = item[&quot;brand&quot;]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0116","card":"q-python-automation-028-parsing-a-json-response","sec":"python-automation-s029","q":"What JSON shape does the UPC lookup API return?","a":"<p><code>{\"items\": [{\"title\": ..., \"brand\": ..., \"description\": ...}]}</code></p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0117","card":"q-python-automation-028-parsing-a-json-response","sec":"python-automation-s029","q":"How do you look up several UPC codes in a loop and print each title?","a":"<p>Loop over the list and pass each code in <code>params</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>for upc in upcs:\n    response = requests.get(base_url, params={&quot;upc&quot;: upc})\n    data = json.loads(response.text)\n    print(data[&quot;items&quot;][0][&quot;title&quot;])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0118","card":"q-python-automation-028-parsing-a-json-response","sec":"python-automation-s029","q":"What is the shortcut for <code>json.loads(response.text)</code> in <code>requests</code>, and how do you avoid <code>KeyError</code> on optional fields?","a":"<p><code>response.json()</code> is the shortcut. Use <code>.get(\"price\", \"N/A\")</code> for optional fields to avoid <code>KeyError</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0119","card":"q-python-automation-029-http-methods-and-status-codes","sec":"python-automation-s030","q":"What do the HTTP methods GET, POST, PUT and DELETE do?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>GET</td><td>Retrieve data</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>POST</td><td>Create data</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>PUT</td><td>Update data</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>DELETE</td><td>Remove data</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0120","card":"q-python-automation-029-http-methods-and-status-codes","sec":"python-automation-s030","q":"How do you send a POST request with a JSON body using <code>requests</code>?","a":"<p>Pass a dict as <code>json</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>response = requests.post(url, json={&quot;name&quot;: &quot;John&quot;, &quot;email&quot;: &quot;john@example.com&quot;})</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0121","card":"q-python-automation-029-http-methods-and-status-codes","sec":"python-automation-s030","q":"What do the HTTP status codes 200, 400, 401, 404 and 500 mean, and what should you do?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Code</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Action</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>200</td><td>Success</td><td>Process data</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>400</td><td>Bad request</td><td>Check parameters</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>401</td><td>Unauthorized</td><td>Verify API key</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>404</td><td>Not found</td><td>Check URL</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>500</td><td>Server error</td><td>Retry later</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0122","card":"q-python-automation-029-http-methods-and-status-codes","sec":"python-automation-s030","q":"How do you process a response only when the status code is 200 in <code>requests</code>?","a":"<p>Compare <code>response.status_code</code> to 200 and print the code otherwise.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>if response.status_code == 200:\n    data = json.loads(response.text)\nelse:\n    print(f&quot;Error: {response.status_code}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0123","card":"q-python-automation-030-robust-request-pattern","sec":"python-automation-s031","q":"How do you write a robust API request in Python that handles request, JSON and key errors?","a":"<p>Call <code>raise_for_status()</code> and catch <code>RequestException</code>, <code>JSONDecodeError</code> and <code>KeyError</code> separately.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>except requests.exceptions.RequestException as e:\n    print(f&quot;Request error: {e}&quot;)\nexcept json.JSONDecodeError as e:\n    print(f&quot;JSON parsing error: {e}&quot;)\nexcept KeyError as e:\n    print(f&quot;Key not found: {e}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0124","card":"q-python-automation-030-robust-request-pattern","sec":"python-automation-s031","q":"What does <code>response.raise_for_status()</code> do in <code>requests</code>?","a":"<p>It raises on 4xx/5xx responses.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0125","card":"q-python-automation-030-robust-request-pattern","sec":"python-automation-s031","q":"How do you reduce API calls and stay within limits?","a":"<p>Respect rate limits by adding delays, and cache responses you reuse.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0126","card":"q-python-automation-031-13-api-keys","sec":"python-automation-s032","q":"What is an API key and why do providers require one?","a":"<p>A unique identifier that unlocks an API. Providers require keys for authentication, access control, rate limiting and usage tracking, and abuse prevention.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0127","card":"q-python-automation-031-13-api-keys","sec":"python-automation-s032","q":"How do you get an API key, for example for OpenWeatherMap?","a":"<p>Sign up on the provider's site (for example openweathermap.org/api), copy the key from the \"API keys\" section, and read the documentation for the required parameters.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0128","card":"q-python-automation-031-13-api-keys","sec":"python-automation-s032","q":"What is the documented OpenWeatherMap forecast request form?","a":"<p><code>api.openweathermap.org/data/2.5/forecast?q={city}&amp;appid={API_KEY}</code></p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0129","card":"q-python-automation-031-13-api-keys","sec":"python-automation-s032","q":"How do you pass an API key to OpenWeatherMap with <code>requests</code>?","a":"<p>As a normal query parameter named <code>appid</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>parameters = {\n    &quot;q&quot;: &quot;Paris,FR&quot;,\n    &quot;appid&quot;: &quot;YOUR_API_KEY_HERE&quot;   # key passed as a normal query parameter\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0130","card":"q-python-automation-031-13-api-keys","sec":"python-automation-s032","q":"How do you check whether an API call succeeded from a <code>requests</code> response?","a":"<p>Print <code>response.status_code</code>. <code>200</code> means success.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>print(response.status_code)        # 200 = success</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0131","card":"q-python-automation-032-keeping-keys-out-of-code","sec":"python-automation-s033","q":"Why should you never hardcode an API key?","a":"<p>It ends up in Git and in screenshots. Load it from the environment instead.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0132","card":"q-python-automation-032-keeping-keys-out-of-code","sec":"python-automation-s033","q":"How do you load an API key from a <code>.env</code> file in Python?","a":"<p>Put <code>WEATHER_API_KEY=your_actual_api_key_here</code> in <code>.env</code>, then call <code>load_dotenv()</code> and read it with <code>os.getenv</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>load_dotenv()\napi_key = os.getenv(&quot;WEATHER_API_KEY&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0133","card":"q-python-automation-032-keeping-keys-out-of-code","sec":"python-automation-s033","q":"How do you keep <code>.env</code> out of Git?","a":"<p>Add it to <code>.gitignore</code> with <code>echo \".env\" &gt;&gt; .gitignore</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0134","card":"q-python-automation-032-keeping-keys-out-of-code","sec":"python-automation-s033","q":"What are the best practices for handling API keys?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Practice</th><th>How</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Environment variables</td><td><code>.env</code> file plus <code>python-dotenv</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Never commit keys</td><td><code>echo \".env\" &gt;&gt; .gitignore</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Rotate keys regularly</td><td>Limits the damage of a leak</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Separate keys per environment</td><td>Different keys for dev and prod</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0135","card":"q-python-automation-033-14-api-chaining","sec":"python-automation-s034","q":"What is API chaining and what are its benefits?","a":"<p>Making several API calls in sequence, where the output of one call is the input to the next. It builds complex workflows from small steps, enriches data from several APIs, and needs little code. If calls are independent, run them in parallel instead.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0136","card":"q-python-automation-033-14-api-chaining","sec":"python-automation-s034","q":"What are examples of API chains?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Weather app: geolocation API, then weather API.</li>\n  <li>E-commerce: product, then inventory, then payment.</li>\n  <li>Recipes: SMS, then text analysis to extract ingredients, then recipe search.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0137","card":"q-python-automation-034-weather-chain","sec":"python-automation-s035","q":"How does the weather API chain get the local temperature?","a":"<p>Step 1 gets the city from the location API. Step 2 requests the weather for that city. Step 3 reads the temperature.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>location_response = requests.get(&quot;https://ipapi.co/json/&quot;)\ncity = json.loads(location_response.text)[&quot;city&quot;]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0138","card":"q-python-automation-034-weather-chain","sec":"python-automation-s035","q":"How does the weather chain pass the city to the weather API and read the temperature?","a":"<p>It puts the city in <code>q</code> and then reads <code>[\"main\"][\"temp\"]</code> from the response.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>weather_params = {&quot;q&quot;: city, &quot;appid&quot;: &quot;YOUR_API_KEY&quot;}\ntemperature = weather_data[&quot;main&quot;][&quot;temp&quot;]\nprint(f&quot;Temperature in {city}: {temperature}K&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0139","card":"q-python-automation-035-e-commerce-chain-with-a-conditional-post","sec":"python-automation-s036","q":"How does the e-commerce chain decide whether to send a payment?","a":"<p>It fetches the product and the inventory, then sends a POST only if the inventory shows the product is available. Otherwise it prints that the product is out of stock.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>if inventory_data[&quot;available&quot;]:\n    payment_data = {&quot;amount&quot;: product_data[&quot;price&quot;], &quot;product&quot;: product_data[&quot;name&quot;]}\n    requests.post(&quot;https://api.payment.com/charge&quot;, json=payment_data)\n    print(&quot;Payment processed!&quot;)\nelse:\n    print(&quot;Product out of stock&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0140","card":"q-python-automation-035-e-commerce-chain-with-a-conditional-post","sec":"python-automation-s036","q":"What are the three steps of the recipe API chain?","a":"<p>A GET with an <code>Authorization: Bearer TOKEN</code> header, a POST with <code>json={\"text\": ...}</code> to extract ingredients, then a GET with <code>params={\"ingredients\": \",\".join(ingredients)}</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0141","card":"q-python-automation-036-robust-chain-template","sec":"python-automation-s037","q":"How do you make an API chain stop when one step fails?","a":"<p>Call <code>raise_for_status()</code> after every step so a failed step stops the chain.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>response1 = requests.get(url1, params=params1)\nresponse1.raise_for_status()\nkey_info = json.loads(response1.text)[&quot;field&quot;]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0142","card":"q-python-automation-036-robust-chain-template","sec":"python-automation-s037","q":"Which exceptions should an API chain catch, and why separately?","a":"<p><code>RequestException</code> (network or HTTP), <code>JSONDecodeError</code> (bad body) and <code>KeyError</code> (missing field).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>except requests.exceptions.RequestException as e:\n    print(f&quot;Request failed: {e}&quot;)\n    return None\nexcept (json.JSONDecodeError, KeyError) as e:\n    print(f&quot;Data processing failed: {e}&quot;)\n    return None</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0143","card":"q-python-automation-036-robust-chain-template","sec":"python-automation-s037","q":"How does a robust API chain pass data from step 2 to a POST in step 3?","a":"<p>It sends the result of step 2 as the JSON body.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>response3 = requests.post(url3, json={&quot;data&quot;: data2[&quot;result&quot;]})</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0144","card":"q-python-automation-037-shared-headers-and-versioning","sec":"python-automation-s038","q":"How do you share auth headers across chained API calls?","a":"<p>Define one <code>headers</code> dict and pass it to every call.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>headers = {\n    &quot;Authorization&quot;: f&quot;Bearer {API_TOKEN}&quot;,\n    &quot;Content-Type&quot;: &quot;application/json&quot;\n}\nresponse1 = requests.get(url1, headers=headers)\nresponse3 = requests.post(url3, headers=headers, json=data)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0145","card":"q-python-automation-037-shared-headers-and-versioning","sec":"python-automation-s038","q":"How do you pin an API version?","a":"<p>In the URL or in a header.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>base_url_v2 = &quot;https://api.example.com/v2/endpoint&quot;\nheaders = {&quot;API-Version&quot;: &quot;2.0&quot;}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0146","card":"q-python-automation-038-sequential-vs-parallel","sec":"python-automation-s039","q":"When do you chain API calls sequentially and when in parallel?","a":"<p>Sequentially when a request needs the previous response (the weather and e-commerce chains). In parallel when requests are independent.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0147","card":"q-python-automation-038-sequential-vs-parallel","sec":"python-automation-s039","q":"How do you fetch several independent URLs in parallel in Python?","a":"<p>Use <code>ThreadPoolExecutor</code> with <code>executor.map</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>with concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor() as executor:\n    responses = list(executor.map(fetch_url, urls))</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0148","card":"q-python-automation-039-rapidapi-marketplace","sec":"python-automation-s040","q":"What is RapidAPI?","a":"<p>A marketplace of hundreds of free APIs, such as text messaging, weather, recipes, text analysis, facial recognition, translation, currency and news.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0149","card":"q-python-automation-039-rapidapi-marketplace","sec":"python-automation-s040","q":"How do you send the key and host to a RapidAPI endpoint?","a":"<p>In headers.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>headers = {\n    &quot;X-RapidAPI-Key&quot;: &quot;YOUR_RAPIDAPI_KEY&quot;,\n    &quot;X-RapidAPI-Host&quot;: &quot;api-host.rapidapi.com&quot;\n}\ndata = response.json()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0150","card":"q-python-automation-040-chain-troubleshooting","sec":"python-automation-s041","q":"What are the causes and fixes when an API chain breaks, runs slowly or gets a data mismatch?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Issue</th><th>Cause</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Chain breaks</td><td>One API fails</td><td>Error handling at each step</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Slow execution</td><td>Sequential calls</td><td>Parallelize independent calls</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Data mismatch</td><td>API version changed</td><td>Check docs, pin the version</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"python-automation-f0151","card":"q-python-automation-040-chain-troubleshooting","sec":"python-automation-s041","q":"What are the causes and fixes when an API chain fails authentication or exceeds the rate limit?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Issue</th><th>Cause</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Authentication fails</td><td>Invalid or expired key</td><td>Verify the key</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Rate limit exceeded</td><td>Too many requests</td><td>Add delays, set request timeouts, log each step</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true}];
